<section id="theory">

<h2 class="section-title">Theory of Double Integration</h2>

<div class="cards">

<div class="card">
<h3>What is Double Integration?</h3>
<p>
Double integration extends single-variable integration into two variables.
It calculates area and volume over a 2D region.
</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Area Calculation</h3>
<p>
When the function equals 1, double integration gives area of a region.
</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Volume Calculation</h3>
<p>
It calculates volume under surfaces represented by z = f(x,y).
</p>
</div>

</div>

</section>

<section id="formula">

<h2 class="section-title">Important Formulas</h2>

<div class="cards">

<div class="card">
<div class="formula">∬ f(x,y) dA</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="formula">A = ∬ 1 dA</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="formula">V = ∬ f(x,y)dA</div>
</div>

</div>

</section>

<section id="example">

<h2 class="section-title">Worked Example</h2>

<div class="example-box">

<p><b>Question:</b></p>

<p>
Evaluate ∬(x + 2y)dA over the region R = [0,2] × [0,1]
</p>

<p><b>Step 1:</b></p>

<p>
∫₀¹ ∫₀² (x + 2y) dx dy
</p>

<p><b>Step 2:</b></p>

<p>
∫₀² (x + 2y)dx
</p>

<p>
= [x²/2 + 2yx]₀²
</p>

<p>
= 2 + 4y
</p>

<p><b>Step 3:</b></p>

<p>
∫₀¹ (2 + 4y)dy
</p>

<p>
= [2y + 2y²]₀¹
</p>

<p>
= 2 + 2
</p>

<p><b>Final Answer:</b></p>

<p>
∬(x + 2y)dA = 4
</p>

</div>

